      "origin": [1, 8],
      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "Walt Bracken sold lumber, feed and seed out of the yard his father built, with his sons Eli and Cal. The Cordon's requisition order came for every board and every sack and nobody ever came to collect. Eli was scratched in the yard on a Tuesday and Walt said it was nothing. Cal took the truck to the roadblock for help and did not come back. When Eli turned, Walt locked him in the office with the safe, wired the old twelve gauge to the door so no one would walk in on him the way Walt nearly had, and climbed the grain leg to the head house with the office key, where nothing that came after him could climb. He wrote his note on a feed tag and sat down on a crate to wait. The shed's big doors still stand open on the yard, and the catwalk boards at the far end are as rotten as Cal said.",
